ar hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the distance between any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side length 6 units, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry of a Regular Hexagon:**\n   A regular hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles. Each side of the hexagon is the same as the side length of these equilateral triangles, which is 6 units.\n\n2. **Identify the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   The distance between any pair of parallel sides in a regular hexagon is equal to the height of one of these equilateral triangles. We need to find the height of an equilateral triangle with side length 6 units.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"288123f80f51382398dec72a0fd431b60fa1508d13a66ebe106532584b1b1048"},"seconds":11.622103452682495,"seed":826206894747762082,"stop":"eos","text":"3. **Calculate the Height of the Equilateral Triangle:**\n   The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   Here, \\( s = 6 \\) units. Substituting the value of \\( s \\) into the formula, we get:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclude the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   Therefore, the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is equal to the height of the equilateral triangle, which is \\( 3\\sqrt{3} \\) units.\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}}\\)"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"3. **Calculate the Height of the Equilateral Triangle:**\n   The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   Here, \\( s = 6 \\) units. Substituting the value of \\( s \\) into the formula, we get:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclude the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   Therefore, the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is equal to the height of the equilateral triangle, which is \\( 3\\sqrt{3} \\) units.\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}}\\)","id":"geometry:95"}
